    <string name="tools_rule_rock_bottom_explanation">Rock bottom: you come up with enough gas for a stressed diver and their rescuer, and never below 50 bar. It is what most training teaches. It is not enough when you must come back the way you went.</string>
    <string name="tools_rule_reserve_explanation">Reserve: you finish the dive with the bar you set. It is not enough when the way back is longer than the way out.</string>
    <string name="tools_rule_ascent_explanation">Ascent pressure: you start up when the cylinder reaches the pressure you set.</string>
    <string name="tools_rule_rock_bottom_always">Rock bottom is the default and is always shown, never below 50 bar.</string>
